---
import BaseLayout from '@/layouts/BaseLayout.astro';

const jsonLd = {
  '@context': 'https://schema.org',
  '@graph': [
    {
      '@type': 'ProfessionalService',
      '@id': 'https://salmonsoftware.nz/#business',
      name: 'Salmon Software',
      url: 'https://salmonsoftware.nz',
      email: 'ben@salmonsoftware.nz',
      address: {
        '@type': 'PostalAddress',
        addressLocality: 'Tauranga',
        addressRegion: 'Bay of Plenty',
        addressCountry: 'NZ',
      },
      areaServed: 'New Zealand',
      knowsAbout: [
        'Software Engineering',
        'Web Systems',
        'Workflow Automation',
        'Software Architecture',
        'Human-centered design',
        'Business Process Analysis',
      ],
    },
    {
      '@type': 'WebSite',
      '@id': 'https://salmonsoftware.nz/#website',
      url: 'https://salmonsoftware.nz',
      name: 'Salmon Software',
      inLanguage: 'en-NZ',
      publisher: { '@id': 'https://salmonsoftware.nz/#business' },
    },
    {
      '@type': 'Service',
      '@id': 'https://salmonsoftware.nz/#services',
      name: 'Careful Software Engineering',
      provider: { '@id': 'https://salmonsoftware.nz/#business' },
      serviceType: ['Web Systems', 'Quiet Automation', 'Human Judgment'],
      description:
        'Fast, honest software and thoughtful automation, built with care for the people and businesses that rely on them.',
    },
  ],
};
---

<BaseLayout>
  <Fragment set:html={`<script type="application/ld+json">${JSON.stringify(jsonLd)}</script>`} />
  <article class="page">
    <header>
      <img class="salmon-mark" src="/favicon.svg" alt="" aria-hidden="true" />
      <h1>Salmon Software</h1>
    </header>

    <p><em>Software should be quiet.</em><br />Built by hands that care about the grain of the wood, the parts nobody sees.</p>

    <p>We live in a rush of generated noise, fragile tools stitched together in an afternoon, abandoned by winter. Anyone can summon lines of code now. Few stay long enough to take responsibility for how a system holds up when real livelihoods depend on it.</p>

    <p>Based in Tauranga, New Zealand, Salmon Software is a small engineering practice dedicated to the opposite: slow thought, clean architecture, and deterministic tools that earn their keep in silence.</p>

    <section aria-labelledby="craft">
      <h2 id="craft">The Craft</h2>
      <div class="building-grid">
        <div>
          <h3>Web Systems</h3>
          <p>Fast, honest software that respects the person on the other side of the screen.</p>
        </div>
        <div>
          <h3>Quiet Automation</h3>
          <p>Taking the repetitive weight off human shoulders so teams can return to real work.</p>
        </div>
        <div>
          <h3>Human Judgment</h3>
          <p>Listening closely to how a business breathes before a single line of code is written.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section aria-labelledby="philosophy">
      <h2 id="philosophy">Philosophy</h2>
      <p>Behind every messy spreadsheet or sluggish portal is someone losing an hour of their evening to work a machine should have carried.</p>
      <p>We believe technology should never demand attention or trap the people who use it. It should clear the desk, steady the day, and disappear into the background, leaving room for judgment, conversation, and craft.</p>
      <p>Tools will keep changing. What endures is <em>care, accountability, and knowing what not to build</em>.</p>
    </section>

    <section aria-labelledby="connect">
      <h2 id="connect">Connect</h2>
      <p>Write to <a href="mailto:ben@salmonsoftware.nz">ben@salmonsoftware.nz</a></p>
    </section>

    <footer>
      <span class="footer-message">
        <img class="salmon-mark" src="/favicon.svg" alt="" aria-hidden="true" />
        Build things that last.
      </span>
      <span>2026</span>
    </footer>
  </article>

</BaseLayout>

<style>
  .page {
    width: min(600px, calc(100% - 40px));
    margin: 0 auto;
    padding: 64px 0 48px;
  }

  h1,
  h2,
  h3,
  p {
    margin: 0;
  }

  h1 {
    font-size: 15px;
    line-height: 1.55;
    font-weight: 600;
  }

  header,
  .footer-message {
    display: flex;
    align-items: center;
  }

  header {
    gap: 10px;
    margin-bottom: 32px;
  }

  .salmon-mark {
    width: 24px;
    height: 16px;
    flex: none;
  }

  .footer-message {
    gap: 8px;
  }

  footer .salmon-mark {
    width: 18px;
    height: 12px;
  }

  h2 {
    margin: 40px 0 12px;
    font-size: 15px;
    line-height: 1.55;
    font-weight: 600;
  }

  h3 {
    margin-bottom: 4px;
    font-size: 15px;
    line-height: 1.55;
    font-weight: 600;
  }

  p {
    margin-bottom: 16px;
  }

  p:last-child {
    margin-bottom: 0;
  }

  section p {
    color: #666666;
  }

  section h3 {
    color: #111111;
  }

  section h2 {
    color: #111111;
  }

  .building-grid {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: repeat(3, minmax(0, 1fr));
    gap: 24px;
  }

  footer {
    display: flex;
    justify-content: space-between;
    margin-top: 64px;
    color: #666666;
  }

  @media (min-width: 768px) {
    .page {
      padding-top: 96px;
      padding-bottom: 64px;
    }
  }

  @media (max-width: 540px) {
    .building-grid {
      grid-template-columns: 1fr;
      gap: 20px;
    }
  }

  @media (prefers-color-scheme: dark) {
    section p,
    footer {
      color: #888888;
    }

    section h3,
    section h2 {
      color: #ededed;
    }

  }
</style>
